            "System work starts with the drawings and the fire strategy. iComply checks which vents should open on which floor, whether the stair vent opens with every floor or only some, and how the system talks to the fire alarm. Where the drawings are missing, the survey builds a simple cause-and-effect table from what is on site and marks the gaps for the responsible person.",
            "Power supplies for smoke control are a specialist area. Standby batteries age, chargers fail and cable runs get damaged when other trades work in the riser. The system is checked for supply voltage, battery condition and charger output, and the cable route is walked where it can be reached. Anything that cannot be reached is listed rather than assumed to be fine.",
